42: under ∩┐╜?oMobile Android/iOS automatic notification handoff∩┐╜?? (2026-10-26).
43: Its existing `app/config.py`, `oaf_interest_service._configuration` and
44: `mobile_release_handoff._configuration` already define the DEVELOPMENT
45: interface: `OAF_INTEGRATION_ENVIRONMENT=development`,
46: `OAF_DEVELOPMENT_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:5055`, and protected process injection
47: of the corresponding credential as `OAF_DEVELOPMENT_RELEASE_CREDENTIAL`.
48: Both `OAF_INTEGRATION_ENABLED` and `OAF_RELEASE_HANDOFF_ENABLED` require the
49: explicit value `1` for a future separately authorized activation. Both remain
50: OFF here. GraManna must run through its existing trusted DEVELOPMENT launcher
51: to accept this loopback origin. No GraManna source change is required; no
52: GraManna runtime/configuration or activation setting is changed by this task.
53: 
54: Provisioning does not inject process credentials, start either application,
55: approve a mobile release or enable any sender. The older activation procedures
56: below retain their separately authorized scope.
57: 
58: `ops/Set-DevelopmentIntegrationCredentials.ps1` is an operator helper for Windows
59: PowerShell 5.1 or later. Run it with `&`, in the terminal that needs the process
60: settings. It resolves the website paths from its own location, so the current
61: directory can be GraManna. No GraManna files are changed. The existing website
62: Python interpreter is required; nothing is installed.
63: 
64: Provision from a separate terminal without GraManna `OAF_*` activation settings:
65: 
66: ```powershell
67: & 'C:\Users\ovisa\Documents\OAF_App\Development\OAF Website\ops\Set-DevelopmentIntegrationCredentials.ps1' -Operation Provision
68: ```
69: 
70: This creates two distinct cryptographically random 32-byte values, represented
71: as 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters, directly in the current Windows user's
72: Credential Manager. It uses the exact DEVELOPMENT Submission and Reporting
73: targets documented in the website README, Generic type 1, Local Machine
74: persistence 2, and the configured `client_id` as the account. Blobs are canonical
75: UTF-16LE without a BOM or trailing NUL, matching the installed keyring Windows
76: writer. Only native Windows facilities and Python's standard TOML parser are used.
77: 
78: If absent, the ignored `config/local/integrations.toml` is created with
79: `[development]` and `client_id = "gramanna"`. An existing valid file, including
80: its comments and client ID, is preserved byte for byte. Existing complete pairs
81: are verified and left unchanged; missing halves, missing metadata with existing
82: credentials, conflicting accounts, types, persistence, encoding or equal secrets
83: block provisioning. There is no replace, repair, delete or rotation operation.
84: 
85: Only a successful readback of both records and metadata produces a provisioning
86: success message. Windows does not support an atomic pair write or a create-only
87: `CredWrite`: this helper takes an exclusive lock for cooperating invocations and
88: rechecks absence immediately before each write. Keep other Credential Manager
89: editors and provisioning tools idle. A write/readback failure can leave records
90: or metadata behind; the failure explicitly requires owner reconciliation. Do not
91: delete records or rerun blindly after an incomplete result. The ignored
92: `config/local/integrations.operator.lock` contains no secrets and can remain;
93: the operating system releases the exclusive handle when the invocation ends.
94: 
95: In the **GraManna DEVELOPMENT PowerShell terminal**, using the same Windows user:
96: 
97: ```powershell
98: & 'C:\Users\ovisa\Documents\OAF_App\Development\OAF Website\ops\Set-DevelopmentIntegrationCredentials.ps1' -Operation ActivateReporting
99: # After the success message, use GraManna's existing DEVELOPMENT interpreter:
100: python .\dev_app.py
101: ```
102: 
103: Activation reads **only** the reporting record and sets these values in the
104: current PowerShell process, inherited by subsequent children:
105: 
106: | Setting | Value |
107: | --- | --- |
108: | `OAF_INTEGRATION_ENABLED` | `1` |
109: | `OAF_INTEGRATION_ENVIRONMENT` | `development` |
110: | `OAF_DEVELOPMENT_ORIGIN` | `http://127.0.0.1:5055` |
111: | `OAF_DEVELOPMENT_REPORTING_CREDENTIAL` | Protected reporting value, held in process memory |
112: 
113: The submission record is never read or activated by this operation. Provision
114: must first have verified the complete pair; reporting activation deliberately
115: cannot certify submission's presence. Conflicting `OAF_ENV`, integration
116: environment, origin, reporting value or unexpected `OAF_*` settings block the
117: handoff. Matching reactivation is allowed. Failure leaves the prior process
118: environment in place; do not start GraManna after a failure. A successful handoff
119: does not validate database readiness or prove that either application is running.
120: 
121: To activate **both submission and reporting** in the same GraManna DEVELOPMENT
122: PowerShell terminal, use the already provisioned pair:
123: 
124: ```powershell
125: & 'C:\Users\ovisa\Documents\OAF_App\Development\OAF Website\ops\Set-DevelopmentIntegrationCredentials.ps1' -Operation ActivateSharedServices
126: ```
127: 
128: `ActivateSharedServices` sets all four values above plus
129: `OAF_DEVELOPMENT_SUBMISSION_CREDENTIAL`, using the protected submission value in
130: process memory. It reads only these exact Credential Manager targets:
131: 
132: | Process credential | Credential Manager target |
133: | --- | --- |
134: | `OAF_DEVELOPMENT_SUBMISSION_CREDENTIAL` | `OAF Website/development/Integrations/Submission` |
135: | `OAF_DEVELOPMENT_REPORTING_CREDENTIAL` | `OAF Website/development/Integrations/Reporting` |
136: 
137: Both records must match the configured DEVELOPMENT `client_id`, Generic type 1,
138: Local Machine persistence 2 and canonical 64-character lowercase hexadecimal
139: UTF-16LE format. Their secrets must differ. Missing or inconsistent records,
140: metadata, environment, origin or existing process credentials block activation.
141: Both records and all conflicts are checked before changing any process setting;
142: failure restores the prior values of all five settings, including absent values.
143: Matching reactivation and upgrading a reporting-only terminal are supported.
144: The existing `ActivateReporting` operation retains its reporting-only behavior.
145: Shared activation never provisions, replaces or regenerates credentials, changes
146: metadata, starts applications or makes submissions. After success, launch GraManna
147: using its existing DEVELOPMENT interpreter in that same terminal.
148: 
149: Use `&` in the existing terminal; starting a separate `powershell.exe -File`
150: process would set only that child's environment. No secrets are accepted as
151: arguments, printed, copied to the clipboard, written to `.env`/TOML/log files, or
152: persisted as user/machine environment variables. Status and error messages are
153: fixed text. Do not print environment/credential objects or enable value tracing.
154: Closing the terminal drops its process settings. For early removal, after
155: stopping GraManna, run:
156: 
157: ```powershell
158: Remove-Item Env:OAF_DEVELOPMENT_SUBMISSION_CREDENTIAL, Env:OAF_DEVELOPMENT_REPORTING_CREDENTIAL -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
159: Remove-Item Env:OAF_INTEGRATION_ENABLED, Env:OAF_INTEGRATION_ENVIRONMENT, Env:OAF_DEVELOPMENT_ORIGIN -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
160: ```
161: 
162: Local Machine persistence remains scoped to this Windows user on this machine;
163: other processes running as that user share the existing credential trust boundary.
164: Activated secrets necessarily exist in GraManna's inherited process memory.
165: 
